{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546959-fiend-s-pact","id":1546959,"title":"Fiend's Pact","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-14T04:28:07-08:00","id":1546959,"title":"Fiend's Pact","content":"Okay, this is going to sound a little weird or even uncomfortable to some people, so I apologize in advance. A hypothetical case, let's say a Tzimice needs to get a very rich/influential individual to be in debt to him, so he makes a proposal saying that he can alter his body however he wants, height, sex, skin color, eyes, hair, everything, in order to try to get a favor from this individual. Now think about this scene and tell me on a scale of one to ten how bad taste it would be? And already going ahead, I know that blood ties, mind control, money, I know there are alternatives, but that's not the focus, what I want to know is how much this scene could be frowned upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T08:53:22-08:00","id":1546966,"title":"","content":"How much that scene is a problem depends on individual tastes and personal projections.<br /> <br /> Remove the supernatural element of vampiric powers and you simply have a plastic surgeon trying to figure out how to get a rich person to owe them for doing a cosmetic surgery for free. On a psychological level they are simply attacking a chink in the mental armor by leveraging either vanity or insecurity. Arguably this is no more or less problematic than most cosmetic surgery advertisements to people who are twitchy about their appearance. If the targeted person is emotionally/mentally balanced, then they won't be susceptible to such an offer. <br /> <br /> So, this really becomes about exploiting the rich persons own issues, but since they are rich then whatever the vampire is offering has to be something that couldn't be replicated by modern medicine, because by virtue of being rich they would have already gotten it for themselves.<br /> <br /> I am quite sure that someone somewhere will have an issue with the scenario, but that has less to do with the content of the scenario and more to do with the individuals views on power imbalance and personal responsibility for choices made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}